# Entry Main: `@: Ref Old\C`, a field of the description, is a reference place and leaves C's parent unchanged
# (#call-receivers: a call cannot supply a replacement parent). `Ref()` runs C over Old and reads Old's x 1, not the
# root's 7. Old\seen 1.
int: x 7
Old:
    int: x 1
    int: seen 0
    C:
        node\seen := x
---
@: Ref Old\C
Main:
    Ref()
